      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In August 1857 the village officially adopted the name Port Sanilac, aligning it with Sanilac Township in Sanilac County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Sanilac%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Sanilac Shores Underwater Preserve protects historic shipwrecks beneath Lake Huron, making Port Sanilac a top spot for scuba divers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Sanilac%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A barn theater in the village stages music and other productions each summer, drawing theater lovers to its rustic stage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
